  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A red bear with a round open mouth throws its grey arms up behind a thicket of grey green crystal shapes, painted on bare plywood.",
    "description": "A square panel of unpainted plywood, its grain visible as background. A cartoon bear with a red body, a pink square snout, round eyes with gold irises and a wide open mouth showing a tongue rises from the lower half. Its grey arms are flung up and out with gold paw pads. The lower half is a thicket of grey, green and blue faceted shapes like crystals or city blocks with heavy black outlines and white highlight lines. The bear and shapes are outlined with a white halo against the wood.",
    "impression": "A bear popping out of a jungle gym of rocks, either delighted or alarmed. The bare wood makes the painting feel like a sign or a toy rather than a window. It is the simplest statement of the magic bear: big mouth, big paws, surprise.",
